      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>The Australian Institute of Technical Training assists students in finding suitable accommodation. Resources are available for rental housing in nearby areas close to campus, with house-share options also available so students can learn to live more independently. Homestay arrangements are also popular for students to integrate into the local community and enhance their English skills. This is where a trusted Australian family allows students to live with them while they study. Meals are generally included, and the cost varies according to factors such as room arrangements, with the estimated cost being between $150 to $200 AUD per week.</p>",
